    "updated_at": "2020-09-24T22:50:52Z",
    "body": "There is an intended change. The HTML standard has its own validity rules that are not related to those of HTML 4. To find out what contexts each control can be used in, you need to consult that control's specification. For example, look at the specification for `button`. As you see, it can be used where phrasing content is expected. It has no expectations around a form ancestor.\r\n\r\nThis is one of many differences between the HTML Standard and HTML 4, so I don't think it's worth calling out specifically.",
    "author_association": "MEMBER",
