    "updated_at": "2020-09-25T01:41:41Z",
    "body": "I think you are now getting at the core of the issue.\r\n\r\nThere is the \"Forms\" section, and then there is the `<form>` element section. I'll try to be consistent and differentiate them as such.\r\n\r\nAssuming we agree that there are use cases for using controls outside of forms, it is unfortunate that control elements are grouped under the the \"Forms\" section. The specific issue I have is that this structure implies controls should only be used as part of a form.\r\n\r\nIn an ideal world, there will be a \"Forms\" section where it talks about forms in general, in which it would suggest using the \"Controls\" to build it (\"see next section\"), and then there will be a separate \"Controls\" section, which mentions they are primarily used for \"Forms\" but also used to build user interfaces. But it is what it is, and it's probably not worth an elaborate restructure just to fix this issue.\r\n\r\nSo then, given the existing structure, where else would you point this out?",
